  "query_preview": "/Monday through Thursday/...\nThe ridge comprising the northern portion of the Rex block will push \neastward early next week as the upper low weakens into an open wave \nand becomes absorbed into the mean southwest flow. Lingering light \nshowers may continue to affect orographically favored areas of the \neastern CWA Monday aided by the next piece of subtropical jet energy \nrounding towards the Southwest from the eastern Pacific. If activity \ndoes develop, total accumulations are expected to be fairly minimal. \nBy Tuesday, deep troughing and strong negative height anomalies will \namplify and intensify along the west coast, however confidence is \nexact the timing and depth of this feature remains low to moderate. \nAs a result, notable forecast temperature spread exists during the \nmiddle of next week, in addition to uncertainty in rainfall timing \nand amounts. At this time, the preponderance of model evidence \npoints towards Wednesday and Thursday as the most likely to \nexperience showers and embedded thunderstorms ahead of the trough \npassage and the introduction of much cooler, below normal autumnal \ntemperatures.",
